{"schema_version":"1.0.0","metadata":{"trial_id":"202610080659-townhouse-row","prompting_method_id":"concept-build-free.v0","model_id":"claude-opus-5-5","seed":11,"server_state_id":"concept-free.v1"},"style":{"name":"Canal Row — three merchants' houses on a working quay","rationale":"The three houses share a stone_bricks ground storey. It is built as two layers: an outer skin at z=0 with gaps left for the openings, and an inner skin at z=1 that holds the glass and doors. That makes every door and window 1 block deep, so the jambs read as real wall thickness. Upside-down stone_brick_stairs at y=4 form a corbel course, and a slab string course runs along the whole row at y=5. House A (timber merchant) has spruce posts standing 1 block proud of its oak infill, including a centre post, and a stripped-spruce beam at y=9. Its front gable has oak verges, an extra west eave course and a stripped-log ridge. A spruce_fence hoist beam sticks out from the apex, with a chain hanging over a recessed loft opening. House B (brick) keeps brick right to the corners, with brick_stairs hoods over the windows and a cornice at y=12. Its stepped terracotta gable rises from y=13 to a 2-wide crown capped at y=18. Each step is capped with a brick_slab that projects forward, and the gable is a parapet in front of a brick_stairs roof. House C (chandler) has a timber frame like A under a flat stone deck at y=13, with a corbelled cornice and a stone_brick_wall parapet. On the roof sits a 3x3 spruce pergola over a grass garden with a hanging lantern. The street front has top-slab paving at z=-1, flush with the floors, cobbles at z=-2 and a stone quay lip with a wall coping at z=-3. Along it stand four lantern posts, at the two party lines and the two row ends; this is one more than the document's three, added for symmetry. There are wall signs by the doors, window boxes on trapdoor sills under the top-floor windows, and barrels with a crate by B's double door. Minecraft 1.20.1 has no dyed doors, so the door colours come from the wood: warped (blue) on A, dark oak double doors on B and mangrove (red) on C, with red poppies on C to echo its door. Sign text can't be set in this schema, so the signs carry no wording."},"palette":{"manifest":["minecraft:stone_bricks","minecraft:cobblestone","minecraft:stone_brick_slab","minecraft:stone_brick_stairs","minecraft:stone_brick_wall","minecraft:oak_planks","minecraft:bricks","minecraft:spruce_log","minecraft:stripped_spruce_log","minecraft:terracotta","minecraft:brick_slab","minecraft:brick_stairs","minecraft:spruce_stairs","minecraft:oak_stairs","minecraft:spruce_planks","minecraft:spruce_fence","minecraft:grass_block","minecraft:glass_pane","minecraft:warped_door","minecraft:dark_oak_door","minecraft:mangrove_door","minecraft:spruce_trapdoor","minecraft:spruce_wall_sign","minecraft:lantern","minecraft:dark_oak_fence","minecraft:chain","minecraft:potted_cornflower","minecraft:potted_allium","minecraft:potted_poppy","minecraft:poppy","minecraft:cornflower","minecraft:barrel","minecraft:crafting_table"]},"placements":[{"op":"fill","from":[-1,-1,-3],"to":[20,-1,-1],"block":"minecraft:cobblestone"},{"op":"fill","from":[0,0,0],"to":[19,0,9],"block":"minecraft:stone_bricks"},{"op":"line","from":[-1,0,-1],"to":[20,0,-1],"block":"minecraft:stone_brick_slab","state":{"type":"top"}},{"op":"line","from":[-1,0,-2],"to":[20,0,-2],"block":"minecraft:cobblestone"},{"op":"line","from":[-1,0,-3],"to":[20,0,-3],"block":"minecraft:stone_bricks"},{"op":"line","from":[-1,1,-3],"to":[20,1,-3],"block":"minecraft:stone_brick_wall","state":{"east":"low","west":"low","up":"false"}},{"op":"box","from":[0,1,1],"to":[19,4,9],"block":"minecraft:stone_bricks"},{"op":"fill","from":[0,4,0],"to":[19,4,0],"block":"minecraft:stone_bricks"},{"op":"fill","from":[0,1,0],"to":[2,1,0],"block":"minecraft:stone_bricks"},{"op":"fill","from":[4,1,0],"to":[8,1,0],"block":"minecraft:stone_bricks"},{"op":"fill","from":[11,1,0],"to":[15,1,0],"block":"minecraft:ston